// A hand-rolled d3-force "force": d3's own forceX/forceY cache their target
// accessor's result once at initialize() time and never re-read it per
// tick, so they'd freeze onto whatever pan/zoom/transition state was
// active the moment the simulation (re)started. This force instead calls
// physicsAnchorX/Y fresh on every tick, so the pull-back target genuinely
// tracks wherever the point "really" is right now.
